# Frontend: Dash

`{{ fp }}app.py`: entry point; `{{ fp }}dashboard/`: layout, callbacks and constants;
`{{ fp }}tests/`: tests. Run: `kiln dev` (or `uv run python app.py`); check: `kiln check`.

- **[LAYOUT]** The layout is a function (`build_layout`), given to `app.layout`: it is evaluated
  at each page load, never frozen at start.
- **[COMPONENT-IDS]** Ids of components linked by a callback are constants of
  `dashboard/constants.py`, never repeated strings.
- **[CALLBACKS]** A callback is a pure, typed function (≤ [FUNCTION-SIZE]) that receives the
  values of the components and returns the new ones: no global state, no module variable changed
  elsewhere. It is registered in `dashboard/callbacks.py`.
- **[COMPUTE-OUTSIDE-UI]** No computation, no data transformation in the layout nor in a
  callback: it calls
{%- if backend == 'data' %} the `pipeline/` chain of the backend{% elif backend in ['django', 'fastapi'] %} the API through `dashboard/api.py`{% else %} pure functions of a dedicated module{% endif %} and formats the result.
{%- if backend in ['django', 'fastapi'] %}
- **[API-CALLS]** The layout and the callbacks never call the API directly: they go through
  `dashboard/api.py`, which validates the response before returning it.
{%- endif %}
- **[UI-STATES]** Every area that loads data handles the three states explicitly: loading
  (`dcc.Loading`), error (an understandable message) and empty set.
- **[ACCESSIBILITY]** Every control has a linked `html.Label` (`htmlFor`), every chart a title and
  titled axes{% if backend == 'data' %} ([ACCESSIBLE-FIGURES]){% endif %}; everything works with the keyboard.
- **[UI-TESTS]** The layout and each callback have their tests, called as plain functions,
  without a browser. Outside calls are simulated ([NO-NETWORK]).
